Aurora witness, RULE-018. Deliberately unapplicable.
========================================================================

This patch exists to be refused. `verify-patches.sh` gate 2 requires it to fail, because a gate
nobody has watched reject is indistinguishable from a gate that accepts everything, and its first
green would carry no information.

It targets a file that is not in any AOSP checkout, so it fails for a reason that cannot drift:
upstream can move whatever it likes and this will keep being refused.

It lives here rather than under `patches/` because everything under `patches/` gets applied.
A witness in the applied set would be a patch the build tries to use.

diff --git a/aurora/witness/nothing-here.txt b/aurora/witness/nothing-here.txt
